# Gasworks site — Cursor rules

## Project
This is the **production** Gasworks marketing site workspace.
- Stack: HTML, CSS, JS (static). **Preference for future website work / migration:** Astro on Vercel (do not migrate unless the user asks). Deploy/modify this Vercel project only when the user explicitly requests Gasworks changes in that session.
- This workspace: `/Users/jackwiley/Downloads/gasworks-site`
- Vercel project: `gasworks-site` → `https://gasworks-site.vercel.app`
- GitHub: `https://github.com/WileyWorx/gasworks-site.git`

## Hard boundaries
- Work **only** on this site from this workspace.
- The former MissingInAction / `gasworks-site-alt` experiment (local folder, Vercel `missinginaction`, GitHub `WileyWorx/gasworks-site-alt`) has been removed — do not recreate it unless the user asks.

## Conventions
- Brand fonts: Space Grotesk (display), DM Sans (body).
- Do not re-add the footer slogan "Built different. Built to last."
- Capability lanes: Spotlights, Narratives, Immersions → link to `portfolio.html?cat=…`
- Home: media mill + category lane reels; portfolio tabs use `?cat=…`.
- Large video: H.264 ~CRF 21, 1080p, faststart; keep files under ~98MB for git.
- **Copy:** no hyphens, en dashes, or em dashes in visitor-facing text unless absolutely required (phone numbers, URLs, filenames, code, legal brand spellings). Prefer periods, commas, or colons.

## Git
After completing any task that changes this site, commit and push to `main` without asking:
- Stage only files changed for that task in this repo.
- Use concise commit messages focused on why.
- Push to `origin main` after each commit (this repo only).

Revoke only when the user explicitly says to stop auto commit/push.
